Basemap tiles are requested only by the launched application. Leaflet displays
provider attribution. Esri terrain tiles retain their provider terms. The bundled country outlines
remain usable when the remote terrain service is unavailable.

The optional RGB basemap uses Esri World Imagery via Leaflet's provider tiles.
Imagery credits include Esri and the imagery contributors displayed on the map.
Attribution must remain visible in map captures; imagery retains its source terms.
https://support.esri.com/en-us/knowledge-base/what-is-the-correct-way-to-cite-an-arcgis-online-basema-000012040
Imagery dates are independent of LiDAR acquisition dates.

The welcome globe is an original canvas rendering of the bundled Natural Earth /
World Atlas country outlines. It uses no Apple imagery or proprietary globe tiles.
Its reference markers indicate catalogue access; survey outlines come from configured indexes.

